<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="Codecov: Metrics dashboard" id="Codecov-Metrics">

    <primary-label ref="codecov"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Open: <control>Codecov Metrics</control> button on the Project tool window toolbar</p>
        <p>Requires: a project connected to Codecov with a detected repository</p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Open the Codecov Metrics dashboard to see the coverage impact of the current branch and the coverage trend of the repository.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>See pull request impact cards and the coverage trend in an editor tab.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>The Codecov Metrics dashboard in JetBrains IDEs shows the coverage impact of your branch or pull request and the coverage trend of the repository.</web-summary>

    <p>
        The <control>Codecov Metrics</control> dashboard opens in an editor tab.
        It compares the coverage of your current branch with the default branch and charts the coverage of recent commits.
        The dashboard follows the IDE theme.
    </p>
    <!-- planned-image src="codecov_metrics_dashboard.png" alt="Codecov Metrics dashboard with PR impact cards and the coverage trend chart" -->

    <chapter title="Open the dashboard" id="open-dashboard">
        <procedure title="Open Codecov Metrics" id="open-codecov-metrics" type="choices">
            <step>
                In the Project tool window, click <control>Codecov Metrics</control> (the Codecov logo) at the right end of the toolbar.
                <!-- planned-image src="codecov_metrics_button.png" alt="Codecov Metrics button in the Project tool window toolbar" -->
            </step>
            <step>
                Press <shortcut>Ctrl+Shift+A</shortcut> (macOS: <shortcut>⌘ ⇧ A</shortcut>), type <code>Codecov Metrics</code> and press <shortcut>Enter</shortcut>.
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>
            The button is disabled until the plugin detects the project's Codecov repository.
            For the connection steps, see <a href="Codecov-Installation.topic"/>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Pull request impact" id="pr-impact">
        <p>
            The top of the dashboard compares the current branch with the repository's default branch on Codecov.
            The header reads, for example, "Compared feature/retry-client vs main".
            Three cards show the result:
        </p>
        <deflist type="narrow">
            <def title="HEAD" id="pr-impact-head">Total coverage of the head commit.</def>
            <def title="Patch" id="pr-impact-patch">Coverage of the lines changed in the branch.</def>
            <def title="Change" id="pr-impact-change">Difference in total coverage from the base: a green up arrow for an increase, a red down arrow for a decrease.</def>
        </deflist>
        <p>
            Click <control>View on Codecov ↗</control> to open the head commit on Codecov in your browser.
        </p>
        <p>
            To find the comparison, the plugin first uses the GitHub pull request of the branch, if you checked it out with the GitHub CLI or the GitHub plugin of the IDE.
            Otherwise, it compares the newest commit of the branch that Codecov has processed with the point where the branch left the default branch.
        </p>
        <p>
            On the default branch, or when Codecov has no comparison, the dashboard shows "No Codecov compare report available for the current branch."
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Coverage trend" id="coverage-trend">
        <p>
            The chart shows the selected metric for each commit that Codecov processed, oldest on the left.
            Its title names the time range and, if selected, the branch, for example "Coverage Trend (Last 3 Months)".
        </p>
        <list>
            <li>Hover over a point to see the short commit hash, the date and the value.</li>
            <li>Click a point to open the commit on Codecov.</li>
        </list>
        <p>
            When no commits match the filters, the chart shows "No commit history to display."
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Filter the trend" id="dashboard-filters">
        <p>The toolbar above the dashboard has three filters:</p>
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Metric" id="filter-metric">
                <control>Percentage</control>, <control>Total Lines</control>, <control>Hits</control> or <control>Misses</control>.
            </def>
            <def title="Branch" id="filter-branch">
                <control>All branches</control> by default.
                Select a branch to chart only its commits; favorite branches are listed first and marked with a star.
            </def>
            <def title="Time range" id="filter-time-range">
                <control>7 Days</control>, <control>30 Days</control>, <control>3 Months</control> (default), <control>6 Months</control>, <control>12 Months</control> or <control>All Time</control>.
            </def>
        </deflist>
        <!-- planned-image src="codecov_metrics_filters.png" alt="Time range filter of the Codecov Metrics dashboard" -->
        <p>The filters are saved per project.</p>
        <p>
            On the right of the toolbar, <control>Show Coverage on Folders</control> turns <a href="Codecov-Folder-Coverage.topic">folder coverage</a> on or off.
            <control>Refresh</control> reloads the dashboard, the branch list and folder coverage.
        </p>
        <p>
            When you switch Git branches, the dashboard and folder coverage refresh automatically.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Coverage drop notification" id="coverage-drop-notification">
        <p>
            After a Git change on a branch other than the default branch, such as a new commit, the plugin waits until Codecov has processed the current commit.
            If total coverage is lower than on the latest commit of the default branch, a warning appears: "Codecov: Coverage drop detected".
            It names the branch and the drop, for example "Total coverage for branch feature/retry-client decreased by 0.42%."
        </p>
        <!-- planned-image src="codecov_coverage_drop_notification.png" alt="Notification warning that coverage decreased on the current branch" -->
        <p>
            Click <control>View PR Impact Details</control> in the notification to open the dashboard.
            The plugin warns once per commit.
            To change how the warning is shown, go to <ui-path>Settings | Appearance &amp; Behavior | Notifications</ui-path> and find <control>Codecov notifications</control>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <seealso>
        <category ref="related">
            <a href="Codecov-Folder-Coverage.topic"/>
            <a href="Codecov-Editor-Coverage.topic"/>
            <a href="Codecov-FAQ.topic"/>
        </category>
        <category ref="external">
